TEXT -3288 -720 Left 2 !.param b=0.5\n.param m=0.5\n.param t=0.5\n \n.param v 0.9\n \n.wave "l+r.wav" 16 44.1k V(Left-Out) V(Right-Out)\n.wave "bass.wav" 16 44.1k V(Sub-Out) \nBLEFT  Lmix 0 V=V(Left-Out)+V(Sub-Out)\nBRIGHT Rmix 0 V=V(Right-Out)+V(Sub-Out)\n \n.wave "together.wav" 16 44.1k V(Lmix) V(Rmix)\n \n.lib opamp.sub\n.tran 10
TEXT -2536 -728 Left 2 ;Parameters b, m, t control the active equalizer where the letters represent bass, mid and treble respectively.\nParameter v controls the volume.\nChange these parameters around to see the equalizer and volume control work.\nMake sure to keep parameters between 0 and 1 exclusive.\n \nFor changing the input audio: \n1. Place a wav file in the same directory as the project\n2. Change the directives under V1 and V2 to your wav file name, but keep chan=1 and chan=0\n3. Set the .tran to be longer than the length of the wav file\n \nI highly recommend trimming your audio, as simulation often takes a long time.
